{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1101157-oldest-vampires","id":1101157,"title":"Oldest vampires?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-07T02:56:20-07:00","id":1101157,"title":"Oldest vampires?","content":"Hello. I was wondering, how old do you think the oldest vampires would be? A few hundred years, a few thousand, or what?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12947-enderdragon1201","name":"Enderdragon1201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12947_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T03:19:08-07:00","id":1101161,"title":"","content":"Ancient Mysteries had an Ancient Egyptian vampire, which I think is the oldest example I've seen. Sadly for him, after being entombed for a few thousand years he's basically just a neonate with some odd memories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T03:44:33-07:00","id":1101164,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Would it be possible for a very intelligent and powerful (and lucky) vampire to last thousands of years without losing all of their memories? The reason I'm asking is because I'm currently thinking about making an NPC vampire that has been around since around 2500 BCE.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12947-enderdragon1201","name":"Enderdragon1201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12947_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T03:57:08-07:00","id":1101165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enderdragon1201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1101157-oldest-vampires?p=1101164#post1101164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Would it be possible for a very intelligent and powerful (and lucky) vampire to last thousands of years without losing all of their memories? The reason I'm asking is because I'm currently thinking about making an NPC vampire that has been around since around 2500 BCE.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>If you want yes. But you want to make the character believable within the context of the game's mechanics, you should probably avoid giving the character photographic memory, an unerring knowledge of all things historical and technological, and include periods of inactivity where his blood potency goes up and down, and some plausible explanations as to how he wasn't killed in all that time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T04:06:11-07:00","id":1101170,"title":"","content":"I should have added, that character was in 1e where the Fog of Eternity was a big deal (though by Ancient Mysteries less so). As of 2e, Fog of Eternity isn't a part of the game any more, so you can have their memories be as coherent as you like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T06:03:46-07:00","id":1101191,"title":"","content":"Well his memory shouldn't be perfect or anything as of 2ed. After all he lived for thousands of years so he probably forgot more then most people will ever know. However in terms of being lucid(as much as elder vampire can be) and his powers being intact he should be fine. <br /> <br /> Prince in my current game dates back to roman conquest of gaul. He has whole floors in elysium dedicated to memorabilia","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12924-orzhov","name":"Orzhov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T06:35:33-07:00","id":1101199,"title":"","content":"The Unholy is another example of a 1e vampire of incredible age... as is Zagreus--both from Night Horrors: Immortal Sinners. Of course The Unholy survived by being a diabolist terror. That aside, the reason elders in Requiem are scary is not because they have 6+ dots in disciplines (though they could have 6+ in skills!), but because they have had time to accumulate resources and develop unknown powers during periods of higher Blood Potency. Note that you don't lose access to your purchased abilities once BP drops from Torpor--you only lose the ability to buy more of them until it goes up again!<br /> <br /> On resources: we're talking about favors, contacts, knowledge and money. Money is a proxy for time and for domain; time is of course a precious thing each night, to be spent in ways that assure safety and security and power (which leads to the previous two). Domain equals blood, safety and security. An elder who doesn't recognize the value of money in managing her unlife is going to have a harder, much more feral existence.<br /> <br /> Now, you can have an elder who is NOT scary by simply embracing the Torpor angle, or assuming that the poor fellow has only just gotten by over the centuries. Not everyone is clever enough to thrive. Some can only tread water until they forget everything else except a low cunning that sends them fleeing danger.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br /> <br /> Edit: Ok, after re-reading, The Unholy isn't actually that old, but she is a big, scary elder! Zagreus is ancient, however...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12493,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","user":"Khanwulf","date":". 06-07-2017, 09:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T08:17:44-07:00","id":1101229,"title":"","content":"Lore wise I like to imagine that vampires began showing up around the time werewolves and mages did, so I'd like to put them back as far as the Sundered Word setting in dark eras; that'd make them rise around the neolithic era or before that.<br /> <br /> However, mechanics wise I don't see an issue with it. Memory wise I like the angle of the vampire forgetting more than most Kindred will ever know because that sounds terrifying to me. I'd also suggest picking up A Thousand Years of Night when it comes out (I know I will); I'm pretty sure it's supposed to have new devotions and powers for Elder Kindred, so that should help. Clan wise I'd suggest making them a Nosferatu or Gangrel because those clans always felt the most primal out of the clans for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T11:34:15-07:00","id":1101304,"title":"","content":"I've established that the oldest clan in my world are the Mekhet, and the oldest vampire that has been onscreen in my games was Embraced in 2290 BC, followed by a Gangrel from the second century AD. The Mekhet keeps a low profile, the city being her sanctuary while she looks back towards Egypt, but the Kindred who know her rightly fear her.<br /> <br /> In my setting, the first vampire was a Darkness-Claimed human who, at some point, managed to pass on a sort of spiritual infection through the blood to three different mortals. In turn, they each spread their power to three others. That makes 9 clans, 5 of which are extant and large enough to be recognized. The Mekhet, the eldest, were created c. 3600 BC. The youngest clan, Julii, formed in 250 BC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T12:29:16-07:00","id":1101339,"title":"","content":"If we are talking that two things I so far had ironed in my games regarding vampire origins are<br /> a) Big nasty wurm thing I've read up in one of werewolf supplements(don't remember with one) as a creature dating back to pangea and having part in creation of nosferatu. He is slumbering somewhere in russia.<br /> b) I use VII and Akhud mixing up stuff from Ancient Bloodlines, VII book and mummy the curse. VII is the demon Edimmu possesing 7 bodies of babylonian elders while Akhud are his foot soldiers created through meshing together what he found out about Iremite sorcery and vampire blood magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12924-orzhov","name":"Orzhov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T13:45:31-07:00","id":1101357,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/705402-vampires-in-the-neolithic?p=710162\">This</a> is a resource some of you might enjoy if you want vampires back when Pangaea (the realm that became the Gauntlet; not the supercontintent) existed. Though it does imply clans coalesced from a unified source rather than having several independent origins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T18:33:47-07:00","id":1101819,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I'm thinking I'm going to imply that he is Dracula through both his name being an anagram for Dracula Tepes and his powers, though he himself does not comment on it when asked. If so, the reason for him only becoming well known in the 1400s is because before then he purposefully stayed hidden and used aliases. He is going to quite frightening indeed, with Mastery over many Disciplines and Coils of the Dragon. One of the ways he will be implied to be Dracula is that he can walk in sunlight, due to effectively having Coil of the Ascendant at a rating of 6. I figure if Dracula, the guy who started a covenant all about surpassing the limits of vampires, was still around today he would probably be pretty powerful.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12947,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12947-enderdragon1201","user":"Enderdragon1201","date":". 06-08-2017, 09:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12947-enderdragon1201","name":"Enderdragon1201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12947_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T20:29:47-07:00","id":1101850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enderdragon1201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1101157-oldest-vampires?p=1101819#post1101819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking I'm going to imply that he is Dracula through both his name being an anagram for Dracula Tepes and his powers</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Who is this mystery man they call Pete Salucard?</i><br /> <br /> Yeah in the setting Dracula's up and about, though secretive. He's got an heir, too, and a bunch of brides, and there's three major covenants based around them. There's a bunch that are older than him. The whole memory loss thing is less of a given factor in second edition but it can happen. Like someone said above you might avoid having a vampire remember every person they've ever encountered simply due to the limits of the human brain. And once you start augmenting that with vampiric power you're likely to get other issues.<br /> <br /> I think in each of the clanbooks there's at least one vampire that's over a thousand years old. The clanbooks had members of the clans basically strongarmed into finding out more about their clan, and that involved seeking out elders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T20:40:32-07:00","id":1101853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1101157-oldest-vampires?p=1101850#post1101850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>Who is this mystery man they call Pete Salucard?</i><br /> <br /> Yeah in the setting Dracula's up and about, though secretive. He's got an heir, too, and a bunch of brides, and there's three major covenants based around them. There's a bunch that are older than him. The whole memory loss thing is less of a given factor in second edition but it can happen. Like someone said above you might avoid having a vampire remember every person they've ever encountered simply due to the limits of the human brain. And once you start augmenting that with vampiric power you're likely to get other issues.<br /> <br /> I think in each of the clanbooks there's at least one vampire that's over a thousand years old. The clanbooks had members of the clans basically strongarmed into finding out more about their clan, and that involved seeking out elders.</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, that's way more creative than mine. I was just gonna go the cliche route and call him Alucard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12947-enderdragon1201","name":"Enderdragon1201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12947_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}